{"name":"Suburban Dream","hex":"#f0efeb","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"suburban","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to or characteristic of or situated on the outskirts of a city; of or relating to suburbia or the suburbs."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who lives in a suburb.","An automobile with a station wagon body on a truck chassis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suburban"},{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Suburb","blocks":[{"text":"A suburb is an area within a metropolitan area which is predominantly residential and within commuting distance of a large city. Suburbs can have their own political or legal jurisdictions, especially in the United States, but this is not always the case, especially in the United Kingdom, where most suburbs are located within the administrative boundaries of cities. In most English-speaking countries, suburban areas are defined in contrast to central city or inner city areas, but in Australian English and South African English, suburb has become largely synonymous with what is called a \"neighborhood\" in the U.S. Due in part to historical trends such as white flight, some suburbs in the United States have a higher population and higher incomes than their nearby inner cities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hempstead%2C_Manhasset%2C_and_Little_Neck_bays.jpg/330px-Hempstead%2C_Manhasset%2C_and_Little_Neck_bays.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suburb","wikidata":"Q188509"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream","wikidata":"Q36348"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hempstead%2C_Manhasset%2C_and_Little_Neck_bays.jpg/500px-Hempstead%2C_Manhasset%2C_and_Little_Neck_bays.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hempstead%2C_Manhasset%2C_and_Little_Neck_bays.jpg/1280px-Hempstead%2C_Manhasset%2C_and_Little_Neck_bays.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hempstead%2C_Manhasset%2C_and_Little_Neck_bays.jpg/500px-Hempstead%2C_Manhasset%2C_and_Little_Neck_bays.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHempstead%2C_Manhasset%2C_and_Little_Neck_bays.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Belmont_Court%2C_Monroe%2C_NJ_08831.jpg/500px-Belmont_Court%2C_Monroe%2C_NJ_08831.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Belmont_Court%2C_Monroe%2C_NJ_08831.jpg/500px-Belmont_Court%2C_Monroe%2C_NJ_08831.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABelmont_Court%2C_Monroe%2C_NJ_08831.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/View_over_Griffith_NSW_1